3. Hard-Gated Evaluation

Translation quality is evaluated in two stages.

Stage A: Constitutional Gate

Let:

\Gamma(x,y)=
I_{\text{intent}}
\land
I_{\text{identity}}
\land
I_{\text{agency}}
\land
I_{\text{evidence}}
\land
I_{\text{provenance}}
\land
I_{\text{reversibility}}
\land
I_{\text{bounds}}

A compilation is valid only if:

\boxed{\Gamma(x,y)=1}

If any invariant fails:

\boxed{\text{Compilation rejected}}

No additive score may override the rejection.

Stage B: Quality Optimization

Only after the constitutional gate passes may the system optimize:

L=
w_RR+
w_TT+
w_GG+
w_CC+
w_FF

subject to:

\Gamma(x,y)=1

Thus:

\boxed{
y^*
=
\arg\max_y L(x,y)
\quad
\text{such that}
\quad
\Gamma(x,y)=1
}

The score ranks valid translations.

It does not legalize invalid ones.

